  "narrative": "Synthesis of round 1 evidence, using the signed convention already applied by the controller. The central supported finding is H4: in the screen-quality-eligible population (screen_roc_auc >= 0.90), SMARCA4-loss cells show a strongly more negative composite dependency score than SMARCA4-intact cells. The discovery estimate R4 is +0.824 signed units, 95% interval [0.755, 0.893], and the independent validation R13 is +0.759 signed units, alpha-adjusted interval [0.666, 0.854]. Both are far above the 0.15-unit effect-size threshold and the entire independent interval remains above it, so H4 is accepted and remains under active investigation because follow-up should test whether the association is robust to genomic co-occurrence. The original negative hypotheses for TP53_loss and KEAP1_loss were rejected because their observed raw contrasts were in the opposite direction. I now accept the reversed claims for this supplied dataset: H13 (TP53_loss associated with a less negative/less dependent composite score; signed +0.424, 95% interval [0.325, 0.524]) and H14 (KEAP1_loss associated with a less negative score; signed +0.816, 95% interval [0.746, 0.887]). These effects are large enough to support dataset-level associations even without prior independent validation, but they are direction-reversal follow-ups from the same discovery tests and therefore remain active for confirmation rather than closed. Negative or non-meaningful results include STK11_loss main effect (R2 estimate -0.016, interval [-0.097, 0.066]), ARID1A_loss main effect (R5 estimate -0.071, interval [-0.147, 0.005]), MYC amplification (R6 estimate -0.019), and all three constructed research-marker main effects and tested marker-signature interactions (R7-R12). The STK11-loss by high-hypoxia interaction (R10) remains unresolved/deferred because the high-hypoxia exposed cell is small and the interval is wide; I registered a lower-threshold interaction refinement to determine whether it was underpowered. The most informative next analyses are the proposed overlap-adjusted or stratum-restricted comparisons, especially SMARCA4-loss effects among ARID1A-intact, TP53-intact, or KEAP1-intact cells, and TP53/KEAP1 loss effects among cells lacking the other correlated loss. These do not test causality, but they address whether the accepted composite-score associations are likely to be direct marker-specific dataset patterns or partly reflect correlated molecular background. All conclusions are associations in this dataset only; biological interpretation, causal inference, and external generalizability remain uncertain.",
  "research_notes": "Round 1 synthesis. Accepted/validated primary finding: H4 SMARCA4_loss negative composite dependency score, discovery R4 +0.824 [0.755,0.893], validation R13 +0.759 [0.666,0.854]. Accepted in-dataset but not yet independently validated: H13 TP53_loss positive score R1 +0.424 [0.325,0.524]; H14 KEAP1_loss positive score R3 +0.816 [0.746,0.887]. Original negative claims H1/H3 remain rejected because direction was wrong. Meaningful-negative evidence against other tested binary predictors: H2 STK11_loss, H5 ARID1A_loss, H6 MYC_amplification, H7 research_marker_d, H8 research_marker_e, H9 research_marker_f, H11 marker_d signature_a interaction, H12 marker_e signature_b interaction. H10 STK11/hypoxia interaction deferred; refinement uses hypoxia_score >= 0.75 for larger cells. Next priorities: analyze stratified confounding checks: SMARCA4 among ARID1A-intact, TP53-intact, KEAP1-intact; ARID1A among SMARCA4-intact; TP53 among KEAP1-intact; KEAP1 among TP53-intact; then validate H13/H14 if warranted and inspect co-occurrence patterns. Keep final interpretation noncausal and dataset-specific."
